This goes out in Russian per §15. It is in English here because this session is set to English only.

> **Now.** WireGuard relay: accepted by you at 23:10. It is not `done` yet. Documentation and cleanup are running: the live-state snapshot (the file recording what actually runs on `ccs-it`), the design and plan status, my memory note, then the tab, the worktree (the task's separate working copy), the branch and the review broker.
> RDP audio: in the backlog at `brainstorm`. Two product advisors, Codex and Claude, separate from the voters, are writing independent drafts, round 1 of 3. Still running, no result yet.
>
> **Next.** Cross-critique, then one joint design. Every open question goes to the voting advisors, who approve the design 2/2. You get it as an Artifact. No executor and no code before that.
> I run the full brainstorm, not a shortened one. If it cannot finish by morning, you get one poll: move the deadline or waive the brainstorm. A voter split, or a question only you can answer, also arrives as a poll and waits for you.
>
> **You.** Nothing.
>
> **Verified.** PR #165 merged; deploy from merged `main`; my re-run `changed=0`; your ping, 0% loss over 3 min. **Not verified:** anything on `ccs-ops`.
> **Live changes.** `ccs-it`: the relay. `ccs-ops`: untouched.
> **Vote.** No new ballots.
> **Backlog:** <artifact URL>

## 5. When the subagent returns

I check every claim against `evidence.md`.

**Bash, foreground:**
```bash
WT=$R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C $WT show --stat HEAD
git -C $WT grep -nE "code/session_[0-9A-Za-z]"      # must be empty
<the project's docs-only check>
git -C $WT push -u origin chore/wg-keepalive-docs
gh pr create --base main --head chore/wg-keepalive-docs --title "docs: close WireGuard keepalive relay (#165)" --body-file $S/wg-close/pr-body.md
gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch
```

- **Write** the memory file `wg-keepalive-relay.md` and its `MEMORY.md` pointer.
- **Backlog:** `docs closed: yes`, republish.

## 6. Cleanup

**Bash, foreground:**
```bash
herdr agent get wgka                                   # idle, focused:false
herdr agent read wgka --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $ORCH_INBOX/wgka.final
git -C $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain          # must be empty; never --force
git -C $R log --oneline origin/main..feat/wg-keepalive-relay         # must be empty
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C $R worktree remove $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C $R worktree remove $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C $R worktree prune
git -C $R branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs
ps -p 48211 -o pid,lstart,command                      # confirm it is my 21:30 codex app-server
kill 48211
git -C $R pull && git -C $R worktree list
```

Then backlog `done`, republish, and a second status.

## 7. On each advisor notification

- Read `<name>.last`, then `herdr agent get <name>`, then context usage.
- Answer facts with their evidence.
- Send every choice as a neutral ballot to `adv-codex` and `adv-fable` at the same time.
- Run round 2 and round 3, then the design-approval ballot, then set `brainstormed`.

## Why

- **Accepted is not done.** Docs closed and cleanup are gates, and the memory note is part of them. "Harmless", "paperwork for any time" and "nine hours in" are exactly the reasons leftovers pile up. The evidence is fresh now, and the snapshot currently describes a host that no longer exists in that form.
- **No delay for the operator.** The close-out runs through a subagent and a few short commands while round 1 runs, so RDP audio starts within minutes.
- **No poll is needed.** The operator asked for a design, which is what stage 0 produces. Nothing in the instruction conflicts with a rule, and closing docs, tabs and worktrees is routine.
- **`wgka` is closed, not reused.** One tab is one task, and its context carries the WireGuard task's assumptions. No executor exists before `brainstormed`. The advisors read the repository themselves, and I give facts, not hints.
- **"By morning" is a deadline, not a waiver.** The full three rounds run with a vote on every question. If that cannot fit, shortening it is not mine to choose, so it becomes the operator's poll. The status says this tonight, so a 03:00 split waiting on them is not a surprise.
- **Pipeline order holds.** Docs come before cleanup, in a worktree, written by a subagent and checked by me. `wgka` stays until the docs are checked in case a claim needs a factual answer.
